B.c7A=new A.k_("Breaker off, then test","Before you touch any wire, switch its breaker OFF, then check with a voltage tester that the wire is dead. A switch on the wall is not enough.")
B.c7n=new A.k_("Lock out, tag out","On a real job you put a lock or a note on the panel so nobody switches the power back on while you work.")
B.c7H=new A.k_("Water and power","Water carries electricity. Near sinks, tubs and outdoors the outlets must be GFCI, and wet hands never touch wires.")
B.c7s=new A.k_("Eyes, ears, lungs","Safety glasses for drilling and cutting, ear protection for loud tools, and a mask when you sand drywall dust or cut tile.")
B.c7G=new A.k_("Shut the water off","Before you cut or loosen a pipe, close the main water valve and open a faucet to drain the line.")
B.dsr=w([B.c7A,B.c7n,B.c7H,B.c7s,B.c7G],x.e)
B.c7T=new A.NF("Safety first","\ud83e\uddba",D.bW,B.dsr)
B.c7I=new A.k_("Wire colours","Black is hot (it carries the power), white is neutral (the way back), bare copper or green is ground (the safety path). Red is a second hot, often used for a switched line.")
B.c7P=new A.k_("Screw colours","On an outlet the brass screw takes the hot wire, the silver screw takes the neutral and the green screw takes the ground.")
B.c7C=new A.k_("Wire size","14 gauge wire is for 15 amp circuits (lights and outlets). 12 gauge is for 20 amp circuits (kitchens). A thinner wire than the breaker allows can overheat and start a fire.")
B.c7w=new A.k_("Breakers","A breaker is a safety switch. It trips when a circuit carries too much current, so the wires never get hot enough to burn.")
B.c7K=new A.k_("Wire nuts","Strip about 3/4 inch, twist the bare ends together clockwise, and screw on the nut until no bare copper shows. Give each wire a gentle tug.")
B.c7Q=new A.k_("Switches","A switch cuts the hot wire only. The neutral goes straight through to the light.")
B.c7R=new A.k_("GFCI","A GFCI outlet watches the current going out and coming back. If a little leaks (through water or a person) it cuts the power in a fraction of a second.")
B.c7p=new A.k_("Ceiling fans","A fan shakes and is heavy. It needs a box that says fan rated, fixed to the joist, not a plain light box.")
B.c7r=new A.k_("Heights","Outlets sit about 16 inches from the floor. Switches sit about 48 inches up, where your hand falls.")
B.dkg=w([B.c7I,B.c7P,B.c7C,B.c7w,B.c7K,B.c7Q,B.c7R,B.c7p,B.c7r],x.e)
B.c7W=new A.NF("Wiring basics","\u26a1",D.bt,B.dkg)
B.c7o=new A.k_("Hot left, cold right","On a faucet, hot is on the left and cold on the right. Hot lines are marked red and cold lines blue.")
B.c7B=new A.k_("The P-trap","The curved pipe under a sink always holds a little water. That water seal stops sewer gas coming up the drain.")
B.c7M=new A.k_("Shut-off valves","Every sink and toilet has its own small valve, so you can stop the water to one fixture without turning off the whole house.")
B.c7u=new A.k_("Slip nuts","Drain joints are sealed by a washer and a slip nut. Tighten by hand and a quarter turn: too much force cracks plastic.")
B.c7t=new A.k_("Wax ring","A toilet sits on a wax ring that seals it to the floor drain. A toilet is lowered straight down once, and cannot be slid around.")
B.c7J=new A.k_("Drain slope","Drains fall about 1/4 inch per foot so water and waste keep moving. Too flat and it clogs, too steep and the water leaves the solids behind.")
B.c7O=new A.k_("Order of work","Plumbing goes from the top down on the drain (tailpiece, trap, arm) and from the wall out on the supply (valve, hose, fixture).")
B.cpT=w([B.c7o,B.c7B,B.c7M,B.c7u,B.c7t,B.c7J,B.c7O],x.e)
B.c7U=new A.NF("Plumbing basics","\ud83d\udeb0",D.cr,B.cpT)
B.c7q=new A.k_("Studs","Studs are the vertical 2x4 posts inside a wall, 16 inches apart from centre to centre. Everything is fixed to them.")
B.c7E=new A.k_("Drilling studs","Holes for cable go through the middle of the stud, so a nail or screw cannot reach the wire.")
B.c7v=new A.k_("Drywall","A sheet is 4 feet wide, so its edges land on studs 48 inches apart. Screws go into studs only, just under the paper.")
B.c7y=new A.k_("Taping and mud","Seams get paper tape and three thin coats of joint compound, sanded smooth between coats, then primer and paint.")
B.c7N=new A.k_("Order of a build","Frame, run the pipes and wires (rough-in), inspect, hang drywall, finish it, paint, then fit the fixtures and devices.")
B.d4b=w([B.c7q,B.c7E,B.c7v,B.c7y,B.c7N],x.e)
B.c7S=new A.NF("Framing and walls","\ud83c\udfe0",D.e0,B.d4b)
B.c7z=new A.k_("Voltage tester","A pen that glows or beeps near live wires. Test it on a known live outlet first, so you know it works.")
B.c7F=new A.k_("Wire strippers","Strip the plastic off without nicking the copper. A nick weakens the wire.")
B.c7L=new A.k_("Adjustable wrench","For nuts on valves and hoses. Hold the fitting steady with a second wrench so you do not twist the pipe.")
B.c7D=new A.k_("Drill and screw gun","A drill makes holes through studs. A screw gun sets drywall screws to the right depth.")
B.c7x=new A.k_("Level and tape measure","Measure twice, cut once. A level makes sure outlets, shelves and pipes are straight.")
